Deployment Instructions
1. Initialize Terraform
Initialize the working directory and install the required AWS provider plugin:

Bash
terraform init
2. Review Execution Plan
Generate and inspect the execution plan:

Bash
terraform plan
3. Deploy Infrastructure
Apply the configuration to provision the OpenSearch domain:

Bash
terraform apply -auto-approve
Note: OpenSearch domain creation typically takes several minutes to complete on AWS.

4. Verify State
Ensure that the deployed infrastructure matches the configuration and no pending updates remain:

Bash
terraform plan
Expected Output: No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.

State Recovery / Import (If Interrupted)
If the deployment process is interrupted while the resource already exists in AWS, import the resource into state:

Bash
terraform import aws_opensearch_domain.nautilus_es nautilus-es
